---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro'
---

<Layout 
  title="Interstellar Medium Cheat Sheet | Free Gas, Dust, Star Formation"
  description="Complete interstellar medium cheat sheet with gas, dust, and star formation. Free download for physics students."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>Interstellar Medium<br><span>Cheat Sheet</span></h1>
    <p>Gas, dust, and star formation. From diffuse gas to molecular clouds.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Components</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Gas Phases</h3>
        <table>
          <tr><th>Phase</th><th>T (K)</th><th>n (cm⁻³)</th></tr>
          <tr><td>Molecular clouds</td><td>10-20</td><td>10²-10⁶</td></tr>
          <tr><td>HI (neutral)</td><td>100</td><td>20-50</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Warm ionized</td><td>8,000</td><td>0.1</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Hot ionized</td><td>10⁶</td><td>10⁻³</td></tr>
        </table>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Dust</h3>
        <pre><code>Silicate grains: 0.1-1 μm
Carbon grains: graphite, amorphous
Ice mantles: H₂O, CO, CO₂
Dust/gas ratio: ~ 1/100 by mass</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Observations</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Emission Mechanisms</h3>
        <pre><code>21 cm line: HI (spin-flip transition)
CO lines: molecular clouds (tracer)
Hα emission: ionized hydrogen (HII regions)
Infrared: dust thermal emission
X-ray: hot gas</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Star Formation</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Jeans Instability</h3>
        <pre><code>M_J = (5kT/Gμm_H)^(3/2) (3/4πρ)^(1/2)
Cloud collapses if M > M_J
Jeans length: minimum collapse size
Trigger: shocks, spiral density waves</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Star Formation Rate</h3>
        <pre><code>SFR ~ 1-10 M_sun/yr (Milky Way)
Efficiency: ~ 1-2% per free-fall time
Initial mass function: Salpeter/Miller-Scalo
Embedded phase: protostar in cocoon</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Download</h2>
    <p>Print this page or save as PDF for quick reference.</p>
    <p><strong>Tip:</strong> Use Ctrl+P (Cmd+P on Mac) to print or save as PDF.</p>
  </section>
</Layout>
